// RUN: not tir prove %s 2>&1 | filecheck %s

// The induction relates the ports and the produced values of the loops on
// the two sides. A term wrapped around a loop would be compared at the port's
// value instead of the loop's, which proves nothing about the loop, and a
// loop that is not the whole side is refused before any proof runs. This rule
// would otherwise be proven while false: the loop carries `x + 1` and leaves
// `x + 2`, so the left-hand side is `x + 1`, not `x`.

rule bad-nonroot: #if(#ult(#sub(#loop(#add(x: int<8>, const<8>(1)), #port(l: int<8>), #add(#port(l), const<8>(1)), p: int<1>), x), const<8>(2)), x, #add(x, const<8>(1))) : int<8> => x;

// CHECK: a `#loop` must be the whole side it is on
